#+TITLE: EPURE diagnostic jobs do not qualify native process closure
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: test
#+DEPENDS: native-windows-validation
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-11-02

* Confirmed gaps
verify-epure-windows.ps1 counts a missing marker only when CLI exit is zero;
nonzero exits and labels ending with an explicit mode can escape its verdict.
verify-epure-api.ps1 counts Ts without requiring exit zero, and Wait-NoCad
force-stops all CAD instances instead of just its owned invocation. These
older diagnostic jobs cannot establish successful native lifecycle validation.

* Correction under qualification
A separate verify:epure-lifecycle:windows gate follows the invocation's COM
identity receipt or batch parent/PID/private-workdir evidence. Exclude every
pre-existing CAD identity, verify account/session/creation and retain a native
process handle. Require both EPURE API assertions, CLI success, kernel exit,
accepted native exit and no correlated crash event/dump. Cleanup after failure
is limited to the captured instance and makes the case fail, even on exit0.
AutoCAD's observed47806 sentinel remains explicit in the receipt and is accepted
only after actual signaled termination and no correlated crash evidence.
MRs labelled qualification::epure-lifecycle get a blocking manual native gate;
other pipelines retain the optional manual job. Existing diagnostic jobs are
not proof and are not invoked for this qualification.

* Acceptance
Run AutoCAD and BricsCAD automation; the COM drawing branch additionally
requires the requested DWG, and the batch-shutdown branch includes BricsCAD
batch. Preserve raw stdout/stderr, full workdirs, identities, commands, code
hash, exit status and delayed crash events as artifacts and lifecycle JUnit.
A failed bootstrap, missing identity/report, timeout, crash or forced cleanup
must fail. Never touch attached or pre-existing foreign instances.
